7. DATABASE AND DATA MODEL

Follow DATA_DICTIONARY.md completely. Key invariants the engine and tests must enforce:

UUIDs · UTC timestamptz · snake_case columns · never plain timestamp.
Every health observation has: metric_code, nullable value, unit, observed_at, recorded_at, data_source, source_reference, status, client_id.
data_source enum: manual | simulated | imported_file | imported_nasa | device.
status enum: valid | missing | rejected. Missing = NULL value + status = missing. Never set value = 0 for a missing reading.
Observations are append-only. Never UPDATE or DELETE. Corrections are new rows linked via amends_id.
Rejected observations retain rejection reason and are excluded from analytics.
Journal body: separate table, private by default, excluded from analytics, audit logs and all third-party services.
Access grants: scoped, time-limited, revocable, audited. Specialist sees only what an active grant covers.
Database-level constraints enforce critical invariants — do not rely on frontend validation alone.
Rulesets are versioned rows. Every alert and every analytics result includes ruleset_id.
8. HEALTH INTELLIGENCE ENGINE

Implement as a pure deterministic function — no I/O, no database, no clock, no randomness:

python
evaluate(observations: list[Observation], ruleset: Ruleset, as_of: datetime) -> EvaluationResult

Pipeline (must follow exactly):

Validate and normalise observations
Remove duplicates per specification
Select 14-day baseline window (configurable; respect exclusion rules)
Personal median baseline
Robust scale: MAD → IQR/1.349 fallback → metric_scale_floor × baseline fallback; scale must always be positive
Direction-aware modified z-score / adverse deviation (direction per metric: high | low | both)
Theil–Sen trend slope + rolling median
Apply all rules from the versioned YAML: single-reading · persistent-trend · combined-pattern · sleep-specific · data-gap
Deterministic explanation with evidence observation IDs
Return: baseline state · completeness · alert candidates · ruleset version

Critical behaviours:

insufficient_data and baseline_forming are first-class states; never produce watch/review alerts without sufficient baseline
Sleep-hours rule: low direction only; 7-day window
Combined-pattern: 2+ co-occurring metrics each at ≥ Noted + persistence on ≥ 1 of them
Data-gap: Noted at 2 days, Watch at 3 days; never escalates to Review alone
Alert deduplication: combined alert supersedes individual metric alerts for the same day
Radiation and cabin-environment readings are context variables — never personal physiological status
Rules live in backend/app/services/analytics/ruleset_v1_0_0_demo.yaml — not hardcoded in service functions

Optional LLM explanation layer (stretch only):

Deterministic explanation always generated first and always visible
LLM may only rephrase structured alert data into plain language — never score, diagnose, create or suppress alerts
Never send journal text, identifiers, raw time series or private content
Validate output for diagnosis/prescription language; fall back to deterministic wording on any failure
Label as "AI-assisted wording of the rule-based result"
Do not enable in MVP if privacy guarantees cannot be established
9. AUTHENTICATION, PRIVACY AND SECURITY
Argon2id password hashing. Never store plaintext credentials.
Short-lived access token; refresh rotation in httpOnly, Secure, SameSite cookie.
Login rate limiting / lockout.
Deny by default on all protected routes. Explicit authorization per route.
Astronaut accesses only their own records.
Specialist accesses only records covered by active, unexpired, non-revoked grant.
No health values, journal text or PII in logs.
Security headers: CSP, nosniff, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy.
CORS restricted to configured frontend origin.
Validate file type, size, MIME and content on import.
Clear sensitive local cache on sign-out. No tokens or secrets in IndexedDB.
No third-party analytics, tracking pixels or unnecessary PII collection.
Audit log: cross-user reads, grants/revocations, exports, alert actions.
10. OFFLINE-FIRST PWA AND SYNC
Installable PWA (vite-plugin-pwa / Workbox). App-shell caching.
Dexie / IndexedDB: local cache, check-in drafts and durable outbox.
Client-generated UUID per check-in and observation; idempotency keys on every mutation.
Write to IndexedDB first, then attempt sync.
Show "Saved locally — pending sync" badge while offline.
On reconnect: retry in order with exponential backoff (30 s → 2 min → 10 min); max 5 attempts.
Server returns per-item accepted | duplicate | rejected — one bad item must not fail the entire batch. Rejected items remain visible with reason.
Crash/reload during sync must not create duplicate records.
Distinguish browser offline from simulated deep-space communication blackout — these are different states.
Clear sensitive local cache on sign-out.
